# Dazzling Theater: "Creature spells you cast have convoke." Prop Room: "Untap each creature you control during each other
# player's untap step" (CR 502.3). Bot1 casts Dazzling Theater; Mind Stone, no creature spell, can't be convoked with
# Memnite, but Alpha Myr is, paid with the Plains and Memnite. Prop Room is locked, so in Bot2's turn 2 untap step Memnite
# stays tapped. In turn 3 Bot1 unlocks Prop Room (its rule applies at once, CR 709.5) and attacks with both creatures; in
# Bot2's turn 4 untap step they untap, and the tapped Mox Pearl and Plains, no creatures, don't.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Dazzling Theater // Prop Room
Memnite
Alpha Myr
Mox Pearl
Mind Stone
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Dazzling Theater // Prop Room.Cast(Ability: Dazzling Theater)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Hand.Mind Stone.Cast(Convoke: Memnite; Mana: short)
Bot1.Hand.Alpha Myr.Cast(Convoke: Memnite)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Alpha Myr.Power = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Dazzling Theater.Activate(Ability: right door)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2; Alpha Myr > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Alpha Myr.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Hand = Mind Stone
Bot1.Battlefield.Dazzling Theater // Prop Room.Doors = Dazzling Theater; Prop Room
